spec: specs/intent-classify.md — a month named alone is a month WORD, not a prefix

why: intent-periods-and-zl (landed today) reads a month named without a day
  by the lexicon's PREFIXES, which monthAndDay could afford because a day
  number stands beside the month there. Alone, «майстер» starts with «май»
  and is May 2027; «лютни», «лютьер», «лютню» start with «лют» and are
  February. Found by okay-chat's measurement over its live turns, the
  evening the parser landed. A month alone must match the month's own
  forms, and English «may» needs a preposition.
